---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="For Organizations | Ethnoir"
  description="How Ethnoir helps organizations understand participant needs, design founder-facing programs and learn from delivery."
>
  <!-- SECTION 1: OPENING -->
  <section class="bg-parchment chapter" style="padding-top: var(--space-xl); padding-bottom: var(--space-2xl); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary);">
    <div class="container grid-12">
      <div class="col-12" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);">
        <span class="voice-3" style="color: var(--color-muted-slate); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em;">For Organizations</span>
      </div>
      
      <div class="col-12 md-col-11" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);">
        <h1 class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5.5vw, 4.25rem); margin: 0; line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--color-tidal-ink);">
          Support works better when it fits the people it is meant to serve.
        </h1>
      </div>
      
      <div class="col-12 grid-12" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary); padding-top: var(--space-lg);">
        <div class="col-12 md-col-9">
          <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-deep-body); margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);">
            Ethnoir works with organizations that support entrepreneurs to understand what participants are dealing with, clarify the question in front of them and decide what to do about it. That might be while designing an initiative, rethinking a program, or looking for where a program creates friction.
          </p>
          <div class="actions-group">
            <a href="/contact?type=institutional" class="btn-primary" style="background-color: var(--color-tidal-ink); color: var(--color-porcelain); text-decoration: none;">
              Discuss an entrepreneurship-support challenge
            </a>
            <a href="/our-work" class="link-secondary" style="font-size: 1rem; color: var(--color-tidal-ink); font-weight: 500;">
              View Our Work &rarr;
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 2: WHO THIS IS FOR -->
  <section class="bg-porcelain chapter chapter-moderate-spacing" style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary);">
    <div class="container grid-12">
      <div class="col-12 md-col-4" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
        <span class="voice-3" style="color: var(--color-muted-slate); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; display: block; margin-bottom: 4px;">
          Audience
        </span>
        <h2 class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 2.75rem); color: var(--color-tidal-ink); line-height: 1.15;">
          Who this is for
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="col-12 md-col-7 md-col-8-offset">
        <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-deep-body); margin: 0;">
          Entrepreneurship-support organizations, universities, foundations, nonprofits, public agencies and others whose programs, funding or resources shape how people start, run or change a business. You do not need to be a business.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 3: QUESTIONS ORGANIZATIONS BRING -->
  <section class="bg-quiet-sand chapter chapter-large-spacing" style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary);">
    <div class="container grid-12">
      <div class="col-12 md-col-4" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);">
        <span class="voice-3" style="color: var(--color-muted-slate); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; display: block; margin-bottom: 4px;">
          Inquiry
        </span>
        <h2 class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 2.75rem); color: var(--color-tidal-ink); line-height: 1.15;">
          Questions organizations bring
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="col-12 md-col-7 md-col-8-offset">
        <div style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary);">
          <div class="question-row">
            <p class="voice-1 question-text">What are the entrepreneurs in our program actually dealing with?</p>
          </div>
          <div class="question-row">
            <p class="voice-1 question-text">Which conditions in a business matter most to this program or decision?</p>
          </div>
          <div class="question-row">
            <p class="voice-1 question-text">What assumptions about stage, growth, funding or readiness are built into our approach?</p>
          </div>
          <div class="question-row">
            <p class="voice-1 question-text">How do participants use the support we offer, and where does it confuse or overload them?</p>
          </div>
          <div class="question-row" style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary);">
            <p class="voice-1 question-text">What does our evidence support, and what should we reconsider?</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 4: WHAT A SCOPED PROJECT COULD INCLUDE -->
  <section class="bg-porcelain chapter chapter-large-spacing" style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary);">
    <div class="container grid-12">
      <div class="col-12 md-col-4" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
        <span class="voice-3" style="color: var(--color-muted-slate); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; display: block; margin-bottom: 4px;">
          Scope
        </span>
        <h2 class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 2.75rem); color: var(--color-tidal-ink); line-height: 1.15;">
          What a scoped project could include
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="col-12 md-col-7 md-col-8-offset">
        <div style="max-width: 680px;">
          <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-deep-body); margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);">
            Depending on the need, available evidence and agreed scope, a project could produce:
          </p>
          
          <ul class="editorial-list" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);">
            <li class="editorial-list-item">
              <span class="editorial-bullet">&mdash;</span>
              <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.125rem; margin: 0;">A clearer statement of the question and the decision behind it.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="editorial-list-item">
              <span class="editorial-bullet">&mdash;</span>
              <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.125rem; margin: 0;">A list of the information you already hold, what is missing and what would answer the question.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="editorial-list-item">
              <span class="editorial-bullet">&mdash;</span>
              <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.125rem; margin: 0;">A view of what participants appear to be dealing with, drawn from that information, with the uncertainty stated.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="editorial-list-item">
              <span class="editorial-bullet">&mdash;</span>
              <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.125rem; margin: 0;">An outline for a founder-facing program: who it is for, the session sequence, participant materials, activities, delivery responsibilities and follow-up measures.</p>
            </li>
          </ul>

          <div style="background-color: var(--color-parchment); border-left: 2px solid var(--color-tidal-ink); padding: var(--space-md);">
            <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-deep-body); margin: 0;">
              An initial conversation establishes the question, fit and possible scope, and may end with a plain answer that the question needs someone other than Ethnoir. Substantive analysis, program design and written deliverables belong in an agreed engagement. Not every problem needs a new program or a more complex tool. Sometimes the useful next step is to define the question more carefully.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 5: WHY RAISE IT BEFORE THE PROGRAM IS SET -->
  <section class="bg-parchment chapter chapter-large-spacing" style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary);">
    <div class="container grid-12">
      <div class="col-12 md-col-4" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
        <span class="voice-3" style="color: var(--color-muted-slate); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; display: block; margin-bottom: 4px;">
          Timing
        </span>
        <h2 class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 2.75rem); color: var(--color-tidal-ink); line-height: 1.15;">
          Why raise it before the program is set
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="col-12 md-col-7 md-col-8-offset">
        <div style="max-width: 680px;">
          <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-deep-body); margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);">
            Three things the Lab would change first in a second run are easier to address before a program’s design, timeline and promises are fixed.
          </p>

          <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-md);">
            <div style="padding: var(--space-md); background-color: var(--color-porcelain); border: 1px solid var(--color-quiet-rule);">
              <h3 class="voice-1" style="font-size: 1.25rem; color: var(--color-tidal-ink); margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);">
                Measurement
              </h3>
              <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-deep-body); margin: 0;">
                Planned readiness change could not be calculated from the baseline and closing measures, so they need to be designed as one pathway.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div style="padding: var(--space-md); background-color: var(--color-porcelain); border: 1px solid var(--color-quiet-rule);">
              <h3 class="voice-1" style="font-size: 1.25rem; color: var(--color-tidal-ink); margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);">
                Recruitment
              </h3>
              <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-deep-body); margin: 0;">
                The recruitment period was compressed, and the cohort was six active founders against a plan of 10–12.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div style="padding: var(--space-md); background-color: var(--color-porcelain); border: 1px solid var(--color-quiet-rule);">
              <h3 class="voice-1" style="font-size: 1.25rem; color: var(--color-tidal-ink); margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);">
                Referrals
              </h3>
              <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-deep-body); margin: 0;">
                The target of three warm introductions was not met. Recognizing a need was not the same as having a referral pathway, so roles should be defined before introductions are promised.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 6: WHAT ETHNOIR HAS DONE / THE VENTURE READINESS LAB -->
  <section class="bg-porcelain chapter chapter-large-spacing" style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary);">
    <div class="container grid-12">
      <div class="col-12 md-col-4" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
        <span class="voice-3" style="color: var(--color-muted-slate); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; display: block; margin-bottom: 4px;">
          What Ethnoir has done
        </span>
        <h2 class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 2.75rem); color: var(--color-tidal-ink); line-height: 1.15;">
          The Venture Readiness Lab
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="col-12 md-col-8">
        <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-deep-body); margin-bottom: var(--space-lg); max-width: 680px;">
          In 2026 Ethnoir designed and delivered a six-week pilot for founders. Six active founders reached the final session. Five had structural business deliverables that Ethnoir’s Founder reviewed and confirmed.
        </p>

        <!-- Fact Strip -->
        <div class="stats-grid" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);">
          <div class="stat-block">
            <div class="stat-huge">6</div>
            <div class="stat-caption">weeks</div>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-block">
            <div class="stat-huge">6</div>
            <div class="stat-caption">active founders<br/><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--color-muted-slate);">reached the final session</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-block">
            <div class="stat-huge">5</div>
            <div class="stat-caption">deliverables<br/><span style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--color-muted-slate);">reviewed and confirmed by the Founder</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div style="max-width: 680px;">
          <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.125rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-deep-body); margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);">
            The Lab demonstrates program design, delivery and review of outputs in one founder-facing pilot. It did not test institutional use and does not validate the proposed application below.
          </p>
          <a href="/our-work/venture-readiness-lab" class="btn-primary" style="background-color: var(--color-tidal-ink); color: var(--color-porcelain); text-decoration: none; display: inline-block;">
            Explore the Venture Readiness Lab &rarr;
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 7: PROPOSED, NOT YET TESTED WITH A PARTNER -->
  <section class="bg-quiet-sand chapter chapter-large-spacing" style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary);">
    <div class="container grid-12">
      <div class="col-12" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);">
        <span class="voice-3" style="color: var(--color-muted-slate); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; display: block; margin-bottom: 4px;">
          Proposed, not yet tested with a partner
        </span>
        <h2 class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 4vw, 3.25rem); color: var(--color-tidal-ink); line-height: 1.15; margin: 0 0 var(--space-md) 0;">
          An application Ethnoir is developing
        </h2>
        <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-deep-body); max-width: 820px; margin: 0;">
          Ethnoir is developing a way for support organizations to group founders by situation, inform program placement and referral decisions, and look at changes in founder capability. It is not validated for eligibility, selection or resource-allocation decisions, and it would not by itself show that a program works. Any use of founder-level information would need consent, privacy and data-governance design first.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- How a partner pilot could run -->
      <div class="col-12" style="margin-top: var(--space-lg);">
        <h3 class="voice-1" style="font-size: 1.75rem; color: var(--color-tidal-ink); margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);">
          How a partner pilot could run
        </h3>

        <div style="border-left: 2px solid var(--color-tidal-ink); padding-left: var(--space-lg); max-width: 800px;">
          <ol class="pilot-steps-list">
            <li class="pilot-step-item">
              <span class="step-num">1.</span>
              <p class="voice-2" style="margin: 0; font-size: 1.125rem;">Founders complete the Venture Readiness Check-In or another scoped process.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="pilot-step-item">
              <span class="step-num">2.</span>
              <p class="voice-2" style="margin: 0; font-size: 1.125rem;">Ethnoir examines readiness stages and main constraints.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="pilot-step-item">
              <span class="step-num">3.</span>
              <p class="voice-2" style="margin: 0; font-size: 1.125rem;">The partner receives a bounded view of participant groups and needs.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="pilot-step-item">
              <span class="step-num">4.</span>
              <p class="voice-2" style="margin: 0; font-size: 1.125rem;">Findings are reviewed with founders and the partner as exploratory support-planning information. Any placement or referral use needs a separately agreed protocol and appropriate validation; the result is not an eligibility or selection rule.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="pilot-step-item">
              <span class="step-num">5.</span>
              <p class="voice-2" style="margin: 0; font-size: 1.125rem;">Targeted support is selected or designed.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="pilot-step-item" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
              <span class="step-num">6.</span>
              <p class="voice-2" style="margin: 0; font-size: 1.125rem;">Follow-up evidence examines capability change and remaining constraints.</p>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 8: FOUNDER EXPERIENCE, NOT ETHNOIR ENGAGEMENTS -->
  <section class="bg-porcelain chapter chapter-moderate-spacing" style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary);">
    <div class="container grid-12">
      <div class="col-12 md-col-4" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
        <span class="voice-3" style="color: var(--color-muted-slate); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; display: block; margin-bottom: 4px;">
          Founder experience
        </span>
        <h2 class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.25rem); color: var(--color-tidal-ink); line-height: 1.2;">
          Founder experience, not Ethnoir engagements
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="col-12 md-col-7 md-col-8-offset">
        <div style="max-width: 680px;">
          <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.1875rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-deep-body); margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);">
            Ethnoir was founded by Olajumoke Michael. Her earlier roles include U.S. Program Manager for Bpeace’s Breaking the $1M Barrier program, where she supported multi-state entrepreneurship programming, and Program Director, Winston-Salem Women’s Business Center. This is her individual experience, not Ethnoir client work or results.
          </p>
          <a href="/about" class="link-secondary" style="font-size: 1rem; color: var(--color-tidal-ink); font-weight: 500; display: inline-block;">
            About Ethnoir &rarr;
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 9: SCOPE AND HOW AN INQUIRY BEGINS -->
  <section class="bg-tidal-ink chapter chapter-large-spacing">
    <div class="container">
      <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl); max-width: 820px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">
        <span class="voice-3" style="color: var(--color-quiet-sand); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; display: block; margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);">
          Engagement
        </span>
        <h2 class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.25rem); color: var(--color-porcelain); margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
          Scope and how an inquiry begins
        </h2>
        <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.1875rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-parchment); margin: 0;">
          Ethnoir may fit when the work concerns entrepreneurship, the conditions of people starting or running businesses, or how related support is understood and directed. It is not a general management consultancy; strategic planning, restructuring and change management unrelated to entrepreneurship are outside its focus.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- 3 Steps -->
      <div class="grid-12" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);">
        <div class="col-12 md-col-4 inquiry-step-card">
          <span class="voice-3" style="color: var(--color-quiet-sand); margin-bottom: var(--space-xs); display: block;">1. Describe the challenge</span>
          <p class="voice-2" style="color: var(--color-parchment); font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0;">
            Describe the challenge: the question or decision and the people it affects.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 md-col-4 inquiry-step-card">
          <span class="voice-3" style="color: var(--color-quiet-sand); margin-bottom: var(--space-xs); display: block;">2. Check the connection</span>
          <p class="voice-2" style="color: var(--color-parchment); font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0;">
            Check the connection: Ethnoir considers whether the work concerns entrepreneurship and whether its abilities are relevant.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 md-col-4 inquiry-step-card" style="border-right: none;">
          <span class="voice-3" style="color: var(--color-quiet-sand); margin-bottom: var(--space-xs); display: block;">3. Agree a next step</span>
          <p class="voice-2" style="color: var(--color-parchment); font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0;">
            Agree a next step: what needs to be understood, what information exists and what a responsible scope might involve.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Closing Note & CTA -->
      <div style="text-align: center; max-width: 680px; margin: 0 auto;">
        <p class="voice-2" style="color: var(--color-quiet-rule); margin-bottom: var(--space-lg); font-style: italic; font-size: 1.125rem;">
          You do not need a finished project or a predetermined service. A conversation does not mean every inquiry becomes an engagement.
        </p>
        <div class="actions-group" style="justify-content: center; margin-top: var(--space-md);">
          <a href="/contact?type=institutional" class="btn-primary" style="background-color: var(--color-porcelain); color: var(--color-tidal-ink); text-decoration: none;">
            Discuss an entrepreneurship-support challenge
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .col-12 { grid-column: span 12; }
  
  .question-row {
    padding: var(--space-md) 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-quiet-rule);
  }
  .question-text {
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    line-height: 1.35;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-tidal-ink);
  }

  .editorial-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .editorial-list-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }
  .editorial-bullet {
    color: var(--color-strong-boundary);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.6;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .pilot-steps-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .pilot-step-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }
  .step-num {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    color: var(--color-tidal-ink);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.4;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 24px;
  }

  .inquiry-step-card {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-muted-slate);
    padding: var(--space-md) var(--space-md) var(--space-md) 0;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .md-col-8 { grid-column: span 8; }
    .md-col-4 { grid-column: span 4; }
    .md-col-7 { grid-column: span 7; }
    .md-col-9 { grid-column: span 9; }
    .md-col-11 { grid-column: span 11; }
    .md-col-8-offset { grid-column: 5 / span 8; }
    .inquiry-step-card {
      border-right: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);
      border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);
      padding-right: var(--space-lg);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .inquiry-step-card {
      border-right: none !important;
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);
      padding: var(--space-md) 0;
    }
    .inquiry-step-card:last-child {
      border-bottom: none;
    }
    .question-text {
      font-size: 1.1875rem;
    }
  }
</style>
